One Weird Dude wrote:
> Is there a Nethack FAQ, for those who don't intend to spoil their game?

I also agree with Ohle - if you really don't want to be spoiled, you
should definitely read the guidebook. Everyone should read the
guidebook, for that matter.

Other than that, you could supplement your knowledge by acquiring true
rumors. Since you don't want to be spoiled, I'll simply mention that
the rumors you find in fortune cookies *might* be true, and that there
is more than one in-game way to acquire rumors which are *definitely*
true. However you acquire true rumors, you should be very cautious.
True rumors are typically misleading or cryptic -- like a riddle that
only makes sense if you already know the answer. If you take some of
them at face value, Bad Things(TM) will likely happen to you. Still
others have plain meaning, but simply aren't very helpful (ex. "Two
wrongs don't make a right, but three lefts do."). Nevertheless, it's
better than nothing. And if you can puzzle out what they mean, the
confusing and misleading ones are often the most revealing.



